From 64a4084b3579b926d2d2ec1574b2ef14de2eea03 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dgabehar <dgabehar@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 13:48:55 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] chat: tool_choice none drops a call for every tag-delimited
 template, in one place

Review follow-up to 8120c3ced, which fixed only the Qwen3-Coder parser and the
autoparser. An audit that re-ran every complete tool-call case of test-chat
under tool_choice none found the same leak, or a parse error, in ~20 other
dedicated parsers (gemma4, deepseek v3.2/v4, minimax-m3, kimi-k2, lfm2, ling3,
ministral3, minicpm5, muse, llm-jp, command-r7b, cohere2moe, ...): each falls
back to a content-only parser under none, which returns the model's call
verbatim or fails on it.

Every template already has a parser for its calls, so the fix moves into
common_chat_session, which the server and every template route through:
- under none (tools offered, no response format) it also builds the
  tool_choice auto params, parses with that parser and clears the calls,
  falling back to the none parser if the auto one fails;
- every call opener (the auto grammar triggers) that is one CONTROL or
  USER_DEFINED token gets a -inf logit bias, so the call is not generated;
- only when every opener is tag-like: a word that starts with `<`/`[` or
  contains a tag, a harmony pattern set anchored on `<|...|>`, or one special
  token. Plain-word openers (command-r-plus `Action:`, firefunction-v2
  `functools`, functionary v3.2 `>>>`) can be ordinary text and keep the
  content-only parser, as before;
- a parser that drops calls itself opts out (common_chat_params::
  drops_calls_under_none, set by K2-Horizon, fork PR #16).

This replaces 8120c3ced's per-parser pieces: common_chat_params::
suppressed_tokens, the autoparser's dropped_call_marker (which could also fire
under auto/required when the template lacked tool-call caps) and the
Qwen3-Coder content cut are removed.

Tests (tests/test-chat.cpp): every complete tool_choice auto case now also runs
under none and must give the same reasoning and content and no call (it fails
on the first leaking template, Qwen3, with the old none parser); templates
kept content-only are listed at the end of the run.
test_tool_choice_none_suppresses_call_opener checks the ban on the repo's
gemma-4 vocab (`<|tool_call>` is one special token there, so CI covers it),
the qwen35 vocab (plain text there, no ban) and, with TEST_CHAT_QWEN_GGUF, a
real Qwen vocab.

Verified CPU-only with Qwen3.5-0.8B-Q8_0 through llama-server: tool_choice none
returns a plain-text answer with no call in stream on/off x thinking on/off;
auto still returns the get_weather call.

